{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active","id":1034994,"title":"Rage To remain Active","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T18:49:43-08:00","id":1034994,"title":"Rage To remain Active","content":"If I'm a vampire who was making a Ambush attack against an elder Werewolf , I Made a Claw against the Elder's Neck to Decapicate him and Scored 14 Aggravated to His neck , And he Scores 1 Success on Rage difficulty 8.. Would he be able to survive this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn","name":"Mkjmn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T22:38:34-08:00","id":1035085,"title":"","content":"They would have their roll to soak and if they make a rage roll to remain active each success heals one level of damage. Depends on if you are making them &quot;regen&quot; the health levels beyond incapacitated or just starting from there. If it's the first they are dead, the second, very nearly dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T00:01:26-08:00","id":1035108,"title":"","content":"By the book, there are not Health levels beyond Incapacitated so the second option <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3198_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3198\" data-vbnamecard=\"3198\">Lunar Falcon</a> noted is probably the most in-line with the text as written. Given the limitations and risks of it, it's also the more fun option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T02:03:54-08:00","id":1035134,"title":"","content":"I've seen it run either way, but by the books only 1 success should be necessary. <br /> <br /> If it helps, it only works that way once a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T03:19:17-08:00","id":1035148,"title":"","content":"Yep, Rage Back counts up from Incap :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T04:06:45-08:00","id":1035155,"title":"","content":"But if that option is what it meant to be like you guys say , You can throw a nuke with probably a 10000 Aggravated And if they score 1 rage success diff 8 , They'd wakeup like nothing has happened maybe gain a scar or two ...<br /> However lets get to the topic , The guy i hit should've been decapicated from the Claw i gave to his neck no?<br /> He was on his breed form He couldn'tve soaked Aggravated in any matter So he took 14 Aggravated directly on the neck , And he should've healed 1 of these 14 Aggravated so he took 13 Aggravated in total shouldn't he be dead? Since his health levels are about 6-7?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn","name":"Mkjmn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:10:12-08:00","id":1035202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mkjmn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035155#post1035155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that option is what it meant to be like you guys say , You can throw a nuke with probably a 10000 Aggravated And if they score 1 rage success diff 8 , They'd wakeup like nothing has happened maybe gain a scar or two ...<br /> However lets get to the topic , The guy i hit should've been decapicated from the Claw i gave to his neck no?<br /> He was on his breed form He couldn'tve soaked Aggravated in any matter So he took 14 Aggravated directly on the neck , And he should've healed 1 of these 14 Aggravated so he took 13 Aggravated in total shouldn't he be dead? Since his health levels are about 6-7?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it works. You did sufficient damage (14) to tear his throat out and kill him. He seemingly goes down (decapitation is unlikely with Vampire claws). (Now they roll Rage since they're at Incap) The next round/action be bursts into Crinos in Frenzy, having healed up however many successes he got. There is more than 1 way to picture it. I was in a game with a similar situation (with a sword involved) and the ST described it as the wound healing as the blade passed through. Either way, same effect.<br /> <br /> Now with the Nuke example, the Garou either has nothing left to come back from (since he is likely disintegrated) or he tries to move, twitches and dies the next round from overwhelming radiation. Keep in mind that the Golden Rule can modify any situation. Generally for the sake of common sense or cinematics. I would also rule the Rage roll kind of hard to use when faced with a guillotine for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:30:07-08:00","id":1035214,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I generally agree with Id's reading. For the nuke you'd either be entirely vaporized or just take more damage the next turn anyway, killing you. As for decapitation, people always want to try and 'game' their damage. And I think this might be a ST call, but I'd have to read the specifics of the incap roll. Did you specifically take increased difficulty (+2 or +3) to target his throat? I'd really like to understand the mechanic of staying up with rage as well because everyone in the Vampire forum always wants to talk about how easy it is to kill a Werewolf for some reason. I could see it as said, 'claws pass through, but heal as you slash, keeping their head on. But with 14 damage, the ST could arguably rule it is enough to remove the head. Again, this without checking all the details on the Werewolf mechanic myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:27:23-08:00","id":1035234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035214#post1035214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I generally agree with Id's reading. For the nuke you'd either be entirely vaporized or just take more damage the next turn anyway, killing you. As for decapitation, people always want to try and 'game' their damage. And I think this might be a ST call, but I'd have to read the specifics of the incap roll. Did you specifically take increased difficulty (+2 or +3) to target his throat? I'd really like to understand the mechanic of staying up with rage as well because everyone in the Vampire forum always wants to talk about how easy it is to kill a Werewolf for some reason. I could see it as said, 'claws pass through, but heal as you slash, keeping their head on. But with 14 damage, the ST could arguably rule it is enough to remove the head. Again, this without checking all the details on the Werewolf mechanic myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think something is fuzzy with OP's math. I have played a 7th gen City Gangrel, and my character never did 14 levels of aggro with 1 swipe. Doing 14 health levels of damage seems quite unlikely unless you just assumed you hit with everything since this is an 'ambush.' A powerful vampire might have a <i>pool </i>of 14 dice to attack with, but that only yields half that number of inflicted damage levels on average plus strength. To deal 14 damage you are rolling approximately 28 dice to hit? What? And if this theoretical vampire is aiming for the neck, that is even less successes that translate into damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T10:20:53-08:00","id":1035300,"title":"","content":"So i will describe the situation and how it was happening , I got a 10th Brujah Who is a thrall to a demon his demon was in trouble as he asked his thrall (Me) To help him , I asked him where he is he told me his location as he told me the situation , As my Vampire was on his way , He was buffing all his physical attributes to the max as he knows he wants to be full ready when he encounters the sept of the werewolves , However My Vampire also activated some visages since he's a thrall on his way , He activated Extra limbs , And Demonic Claws , And the ability to block mental controls from anyone but his demon master , And he also activated His brawl ability from the visage -2 Difficulty for any brawl based roll , So after my Vampire who had 5 Celerity , 5 Potence and 6 Dexterity 6 Stamina 6 Strength went inside he tried ambushing the werewolves , Sadly i tried activating celerity or even using my extra limbs for extra actions but the ST said i cannot do it since it says it's only 1 action according to the book ... So i chose to attack the Strongest elder of the werewolves , I sliced his neck from his back difficulty was 8 Base (-2 From visage , -2 From being over his back ) I scored about 10 successes or something as i remember.. from 14 Dices diff 5 And i had auto Damage from potence as i spent 1 bp for automated potence damage so i had 10 Net + 6 Strength + 2 Neck + 2 Claws.. Which is 19 Dices and 5 auto aggravated over his neck... And i rolled the 19 Dices i scored 9 Successes + 5 (Auto) Gave me 14 Aggravated over his neck , He couldn't soak the damage since he was in his breed form , And he rolled rage to remain active , He scored 1 success.. He said it like this ((** As your claw hit his neck and leave his flesh would recover just leaving a scar over his neck. **)) And then the ST told me to roll initiative as the second turn takes place , I had the third highest initiative since most of the werewolves had spirit of fray +10 on initiative rolls so the Athro werewolf Cried &quot;Protect the Elder&quot; and then i declared investing 4 Celerity Action to claw the elder werewolf 4 times from celerity and three times from extra limbs total of 7 Claws and then the werewolf elder spent 6 rage (He had the total of 7) (And gnosis of 6) and declared To dodge it all... Where it clearly says that a<br /> berserking werewolf would simply pick a target and hit it but all what he did was trying to dodge all my attacks , If there was anything wrong from that roleplay ... I wish you would tell me what's wrong from what he did , Waiting for your replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn","name":"Mkjmn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:45:21-08:00","id":1035344,"title":"","content":"Well, it's hard to call any particular issues with all that because crossover between three games is messy and going to involve a lot of iffy calls no matter what.<br /> <br /> How things progressed after your ambush attack on the Elder seems... strange (also the werewolves can't spend more than half their rage in a turn, so 4 in this case), but like I said crossover can be weird.<br /> <br /> In terms of actual decision making on the RP side of things, I can't really see the fault in anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:50:54-08:00","id":1035349,"title":"","content":"You're correct that the Garou should not be dodging if he's in the midst of a frenzy. Also, he shouldn't be spending 6 out of 7 rage. You're generally limited to half (rounded up), plus his extra actions are limited by the lower of his Dex or Wits. Not to throw him under the bus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Edited to add: Whoops, his extra actions are limited by Dex in this case, not Wits, since he's in the middle of a frenzy.)<br /> <br /> Now, that said, I personally would question some of the &quot;pre-loading&quot; of your abilities, as it sounded like that was mostly handled in a prior scene. Without digging through books and rules, many abilities last for a scene or less. Just at a glance, it sounds kind of powergamey. However, I'm just nitpicking. Much of that can be handled with good RP decisions, but you'd likely have to be hiding first to pull it off (rather than buffing on your way there, X scene(s) before), and I of course have to poke fun at a Brujah hiding in the shadows. &lt;3 Don't take it to heart, though, I'm only teasing.<br /> <br /> Regarding rage healing, as has been said before, your attack happens FIRST, and then the werewolf's rage heal roll happens NEXT. You dropped the Garou initially, no question there. Now that he's down, NOW he rolls his rage. It's a split second difference, but it matters. Soak is simultaneous, yes. But rage healing needs the damage to happen first, otherwise, what's healing? With that in mind, he only needs one success to stay alive.<br /> <br /> If you can finish him off the next round, good for you.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mkjmn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035300#post1035300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">he encounters the sept of the werewolves</div> </div> </div> </div>But, truly, I think you have bigger problems to worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","user":"Wakuwa","date":". 01-20-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:03:17-08:00","id":1035355,"title":"","content":"Question, can the incap rage roll even heal agg damage caused by silver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:12:01-08:00","id":1035365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035355#post1035355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, can the incap rage roll even heal agg damage caused by silver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:20:50-08:00","id":1035373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035355#post1035355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, can the incap rage roll even heal agg damage caused by silver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage healing isn't dependent on type of damage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12843\" data-vbnamecard=\"12843\">Mkjmn</a> One thing I also forgot to add in my previous post: the Garou shouldn't be in a frenzy, unless something different is going on. He didn't get enough successes on his rage roll to frenzy, considering he only got one success. In that case, he can choose to dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:32:46-08:00","id":1035383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035373#post1035373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rage healing isn't dependent on type of damage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12843\" data-vbnamecard=\"12843\">Mkjmn</a> One thing I also forgot to add in my previous post: the Garou shouldn't be in a frenzy, unless something different is going on. He didn't get enough successes on his rage roll to frenzy, considering he only got one success. In that case, he can choose to dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it. I'm not intimately familiar with Werewolf mechanics. It was more a question to gain my understanding, so I appreciate both of your responses. The thing that bothers me about the Vampire forum is they love to continually trod out Werewolf whipping boys and how easy they'd destroy them. So I like to be aware of why they are wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:43:24-08:00","id":1035385,"title":"","content":"Basically echoing above.<br /> <br /> The Rage to heal worked how it should. Your pre-loading scene long powers is kind of sketchy. Crossovers can be weird since calls need to be made between powers. The Elder shouldn't have been able to spend so much Rage. He can dodge fine in Frenzy at the cost of a Willpower for the turn. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035349#post1035349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But, truly, I think you have bigger problems to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very true.<br /> <br /> Be happy your character is alive. Getting an ambush action on a Sept of Garou should still end up with your character dead. There isn't generally a single Elder on a Caern, so even if you has killed that one you would still face multiple others.<br /> <br /> So many things about this scene are questionable (on both sides). Off the top of my head:<br /> Where was this Sept?<br /> How did you know which Garou was <i>the</i> Elder?<br /> How did you get so close?<br /> How did you run away/survive?<br /> Tribes and numbers of the Garou involved?<br /> ....on that note, it could have been worse. A Silverfang Elder could have ignored the blow entirely and left you mortal-ish the round after. There are any number of other Elder Gifts that could have decided the combat on the following round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:47:44-08:00","id":1035387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035373#post1035373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rage healing isn't dependent on type of damage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12843\" data-vbnamecard=\"12843\">Mkjmn</a> One thing I also forgot to add in my previous post: the Garou shouldn't be in a frenzy, unless something different is going on. He didn't get enough successes on his rage roll to frenzy, considering he only got one success. In that case, he can choose to dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for staying active you automatically frenzy, and your successes on the difficulty 8 rage roll are just to see how much health you regain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:57:37-08:00","id":1035391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035373#post1035373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12843\" data-vbnamecard=\"12843\">Mkjmn</a> One thing I also forgot to add in my previous post: the Garou shouldn't be in a frenzy, unless something different is going on. He didn't get enough successes on his rage roll to frenzy, considering he only got one success. In that case, he can choose to dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just reread this section in W20 and you are most certainly correct. I think maybe my first group misread that line and we've been playing with Frenzy being part of making that roll, as opposed to based on successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035383#post1035383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to hear it. I'm not intimately familiar with Werewolf mechanics. It was more a question to gain my understanding, so I appreciate both of your responses. The thing that bothers me about the Vampire forum is they love to continually trod out Werewolf whipping boys and how easy they'd destroy them. So I like to be aware of why they are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, whenever any of the game lines player's sell short any of the other splats it's bothersome. The Rage roll to recover is a big one that's overlooked. Basically, under most normal circumstances you need to kill a Garou twice in a scene for them to stay down. On top of that, most proposed conflicts I see talked about don't bother mentioning the Gifts that Garou bring to the table. That would be like assuming all Vampires lacked any Discipline dots and just treating them with their innate abilities. There are some incredibly useful Rank 1 Gifts. But Rank 2-3 Gifts can be situationally pretty powerful. The Rank 4 or 5 Gifts can turn the tide of a fight all by themselves (sometimes). So the idea of killing Elders offhandedly is usually silly. Just like killing any other splats Elder's (Vampires or otherwise) should be treated the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035387#post1035387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for staying active you automatically frenzy, and your successes on the difficulty 8 rage roll are just to see how much health you regain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so too until I just looked it up. The wording is easy to read that way, but having just looked at it, I actually agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12552_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12552\" data-vbnamecard=\"12552\">Monalfie</a><br /> Here is the exact wording:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20 Page 145</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">However, this last-ditch survival effort has its price. Like all</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Rage rolls, the character is still subject to frenzy. The wound will</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">also remain on the Garou\u2019s body as an appropriate Battle Scar.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Since it says &quot;like all Rage rolls&quot;, I assume they mean for it to follow the general rule of rolling Rage (4+ successes to Frenzy). My first group ran it the way you're (</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">) remembering it, and so I've always done the same.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-20-2017, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:11:33-08:00","id":1035396,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I feel like this might be another edition clash... gonna look my old books when I get home and check. Still doesn't mean I am right, at the end of the day, but it feels like more and more stuff got changed. White Wolf is gaslighting me, yo!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:13:34-08:00","id":1035399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035396#post1035396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I feel like this might be another edition clash... gonna look my old books when I get home and check. Still doesn't mean I am right, at the end of the day, but it feels like more and more stuff got changed. White Wolf is gaslighting me, yo!</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know what you find. Like I said, I remember it the way you do so I'll be curious if it is an edition thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:53:18-08:00","id":1035432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035391#post1035391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just reread this section in W20 and you are most certainly correct. I think maybe my first group misread that line and we've been playing with Frenzy being part of making that roll, as opposed to based on successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yea, whenever any of the game lines player's sell short any of the other splats it's bothersome. The Rage roll to recover is a big one that's overlooked. Basically, under most normal circumstances you need to kill a Garou twice in a scene for them to stay down. On top of that, most proposed conflicts I see talked about don't bother mentioning the Gifts that Garou bring to the table. That would be like assuming all Vampires lacked any Discipline dots and just treating them with their innate abilities. There are some incredibly useful Rank 1 Gifts. But Rank 2-3 Gifts can be situationally pretty powerful. The Rank 4 or 5 Gifts can turn the tide of a fight all by themselves (sometimes). So the idea of killing Elders offhandedly is usually silly. Just like killing any other splats Elder's (Vampires or otherwise) should be treated the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never underestimate the ability to take only bashing damage from fires when you're around so much flammable material in the city. And in rural areas? Find a grain silo and wait for the right time to use Create Element to send it up in a thermobaric explosion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:19:14-08:00","id":1035448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035432#post1035432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Never underestimate the ability to take only bashing damage from fires when you're around so much flammable material in the city. And in rural areas? Find a grain silo and wait for the right time to use Create Element to send it up in a thermobaric explosion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. I do get the impression Vampire-only players don't understand how common Master of Fire is. I really like Create Element for its versatility, but it is much less common (in my experience).<br /> <br /> There are a ton of awesome 1st rank Gifts. Falling Touch is beyond hilarious. Call of the Wyld has <i>so many</i> uses. Mindspeak is great for the debuff of -2 Dice against a big boss type single enemy while the pack goes to town. There are plenty of others, but those are some of my favorites off the top of my head.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:37:53-08:00","id":1035457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035396#post1035396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I feel like this might be another edition clash... gonna look my old books when I get home and check. Still doesn't mean I am right, at the end of the day, but it feels like more and more stuff got changed. White Wolf is gaslighting me, yo!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haha! I think you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a> have the right of it. I try to go by W20 these days for simplicity's sake (unless it doesn't yield the answer, or we're pulling some Gift that hasn't been updated), so that's what's on the forefront of my mind when thinking about the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T14:46:37-08:00","id":1035464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035383#post1035383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to hear it. I'm not intimately familiar with Werewolf mechanics. It was more a question to gain my understanding, so I appreciate both of your responses. The thing that bothers me about the Vampire forum is they love to continually trod out Werewolf whipping boys and how easy they'd destroy them. So I like to be aware of why they are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't think there's one easy answer to that question. One vampire against one Garou will greatly depend on each individual (though ranks being equal, I would generally put my money on the Garou, though this is still a gamble). One vamp against a pack leans heavily toward the Garou, but even that's not a certainty. Multiple leeches against one Garou can also go any which way, though probably favors the vampires (so long as we're not talking Rank 1 vampires against a Rank 5 Garou, as a very extreme example). It really comes down to the individuals and the situation. The simple answer I've heard is, &quot;Yes, but you rarely get the chance to fight just -one- Garou,&quot; and that's very true.<br /> <br /> Most of the poo-flinging just seems to happen because someone is trying to promote their favorite monster as &quot;the best.&quot; Though, to be fair, if you round up some die-hard Werewolf players, you're gonna get the exact same arguing on a smaller scale. They'll be at each other's throats over tribal loyalties. So it goes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:00:48-08:00","id":1035474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035464#post1035464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I don't think there's one easy answer to that question. One vampire against one Garou will greatly depend on each individual (though ranks being equal, I would generally put my money on the Garou, though this is still a gamble). One vamp against a pack leans heavily toward the Garou, but even that's not a certainty. Multiple leeches against one Garou can also go any which way, though probably favors the vampires (so long as we're not talking Rank 1 vampires against a Rank 5 Garou, as a very extreme example). It really comes down to the individuals and the situation. The simple answer I've heard is, &quot;Yes, but you rarely get the chance to fight just -one- Garou,&quot; and that's very true.<br /> <br /> Most of the poo-flinging just seems to happen because someone is trying to promote their favorite monster as &quot;the best.&quot; Though, to be fair, if you round up some die-hard Werewolf players, you're gonna get the exact same arguing on a smaller scale. They'll be at each other's throats over tribal loyalties. So it goes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>+1 to all of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T15:10:40-08:00","id":1035479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035464#post1035464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rank 1 vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't have Rank. Rank is a terribly difficult to raise special Status Background mixed in with the Self-Control Virtue and an abstract version of Armory, which hinges on spirits knowing and celebrating your past deeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:07:53-08:00","id":1035499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035479#post1035479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires don't have Rank. Rank is a terribly difficult to raise special Status Background mixed in with the Self-Control Virtue and an abstract version of Armory, which hinges on spirits knowing and celebrating your past deeds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoops, yup, unholy error on my part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though I hope my meaning was still clear. (It's been since the 90s since I've played Vampire.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:35:38-08:00","id":1035547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035499#post1035499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Whoops, yup, unholy error on my part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though I hope my meaning was still clear. (It's been since the 90s since I've played Vampire.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood and decided not to nitpick \ud83d\ude00","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:05:59-08:00","id":1035712,"title":"","content":"Well, I my Wild West book is word-for-word what Idpersona posted, and that book borrowed a lot of 2nd Ed. So I guess we have been playing it wrong...<br /> <br /> tl;dr everything I know is a lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:35:57-08:00","id":1035716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035712#post1035712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I my Wild West book is word-for-word what Idpersona posted, and that book borrowed a lot of 2nd Ed. So I guess we have been playing it wrong...<br /> <br /> tl;dr everything I know is a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checked Revised and it was worded the same way. 2nd Ed was worded differently, but amounts to the same thing.<br /> <br /> Now we must hang our heads in shame and abandon the game, because we were wrong about a minor rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:56:44-08:00","id":1035722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035716#post1035716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just checked Revised and it was worded the same way. 2nd Ed was worded differently, but amounts to the same thing.<br /> <br /> Now we must hang our heads in shame and abandon the game, because we were wrong about a minor rule. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is a slippery slope, man. First I forget how 'remain active' works, next thing you know I'm forgetting the recipe for a PB&amp;J sandwich!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T19:54:17-08:00","id":1035924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035722#post1035722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a slippery slope, man. First I forget how 'remain active' works, next thing you know I'm forgetting the recipe for a PB&amp;J sandwich!</div> </div> </div> </div>(Bites into sandwich, noting odd taste)<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait a minute, this PB&amp;J is... plum butter and jello? ALL IS LOST! NOTHING MAKES SENSE ANYMORE! WHY COULDN'T WE REMEMBER OUR OWN RULES?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T21:10:49-08:00","id":1035942,"title":"","content":"W20 contradicts itself with the rules regarding a Garou entering frenzy upon rolling to remain active. Page 256 &quot;A critically injured werewolf can channel her Rage to save her life. It's a risky proposition- if it succeeds, the werewolf is thrown into a wild frenzy. It's sometimes the only way for a character to save her life,though. To remain active, the player rolls his character's permanent Rage (difficulty 8). Each success heals one health level of any kind of damage. No matter how much damage is healed, the character enters a berserk frenzy.&quot;<br /> <br /> The example below then has the player manage three successes and go into a berserk frenzy at the start of their next turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:19:42-08:00","id":1036110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1034994-rage-to-remain-active?p=1035942#post1035942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 contradicts itself with the rules regarding a Garou entering frenzy upon rolling to remain active. Page 256 &quot;A critically injured werewolf can channel her Rage to save her life. It's a risky proposition- if it succeeds, the werewolf is thrown into a wild frenzy. It's sometimes the only way for a character to save her life,though. To remain active, the player rolls his character's permanent Rage (difficulty 8). Each success heals one health level of any kind of damage. No matter how much damage is healed, the character enters a berserk frenzy.&quot;<br /> <br /> The example below then has the player manage three successes and go into a berserk frenzy at the start of their next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>And balance is restored in the universe. &lt;3 Haha!<br /> <br /> Seriously, thanks for finding/posting this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:32:21-08:00","id":1036121,"title":"","content":"Yep. Thank you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"P